.TH SSH-CLI 1 "August 2026" "ssh-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssh-cli \- multi-endpoint SSH command-line client (Rust core)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh-cli
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B ssh-cli
[\fB\-\-json\fR] \fBconfig \-\-check\fR \fIpath\fR
.br
.B ssh-cli
\fBcap\fR \fBforward\fR \fB\-\-listen\fR \fIip:port\fR \fB\-\-target\fR \fIhost:port\fR
.br
.B ssh-cli
\fBcap\fR \fBsftp\fR
.br
.B ssh-cli
\fBcap\fR \fBproxy \-\-chain\fR \fIspec\fR \fB\-\-target\fR \fIhost\fR [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ssh-cli connects to hosts through the shared Rust core (SSH, SFTP, port
forwarding, proxy chains). Commands share the same engines as the GUI so
behavior never diverges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit machine-readable, versioned JSON (schema_version 1) instead of
human text.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config \-\-check \fIpath\fR
Validate a host-alias configuration file.
.TP
.B cap forward \-\-listen \fIip:port\fR \-\-target \fIhost:port\fR
Print the local-forwarding spec (shared core config).
.TP
.B cap sftp
Print the streaming-transfer spec (shared core config).
.TP
.B cap proxy \-\-chain \fIspec\fR \-\-target \fIhost\fR [\-\-port \fIport\fR]
Validate a proxy chain and print the first-hop SOCKS5 wire bytes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected internal error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad arguments).
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 4
Connection error.
.TP
.B 5
Remote command failed.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
Every JSON payload carries "schema_version": 1. See
cli-output.schema.json for the schema.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
